  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This is a request to have a tab in the default menu system for 'World Features,' that can be customized by world creators, such as through Udon.\n\nAt present, if a world creator wishes to provide options to a player for lighting, sound, etc. one of three approaches is usually taken:\n\n1. Menus placed at specific locations throughout the world\n\n2. Tablet-style menus that must be carried by the player\n\n3. A menu that can be summoned through a specific controller input\n\nThe first presents an issue of players needing to find & navigate to a specific location to edit world settings; \n\nthe second can be cumbersome as it requires finding & carrying an object; \n\nand the third often conflicts with players' controller bindings, leading to menus being summoned when they aren't desired.\n\nA world creator customizable 'world features' tab in the default menu would circumvent all of these issues- features of the world could be controlled from everywhere, with an interface action that is already accommodated for by standard controls.",
